{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>On the day of anointing him.</b> The bet stands in place of a mem — the meaning is: from the day they anointed him, he is obligated to bring this meal-offering. Compare: <b>ביום משחו אותם</b> — the meaning is 'from the day he anointed them.' And similarly: <b>והנותר בבשר ובלחם</b> — the meaning is 'from the meat and from the bread.'" "<b>Half of it in the morning and half of it in the evening.</b> How does he do it? He brings a whole tenth of an ephah and halves it, and offers half of it in the morning and half of it between the evenings. If half of the afternoon offering became impure or was lost, he brings a whole tenth of an ephah and halves it, and offers half and half. It turns out that two halves are offered and two halves are lost."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The lemma's bet in ביום is argued to have the force of מן 'from'; the examples from Num 7:84 (ביום משחו) and Lev 8:32 (והנותר) illustrate the same usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:18.263954061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}